#: includes/trips-proxy.php:1321
#, php-format
msgid "Nothing was saved: %s. The text below is the one that was sent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/trips-proxy.php:1336
msgid "Only the scheme and the domain of the address were kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/trips-proxy.php:1339
msgid "The address is http: the links travel unencrypted between this server and the installation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/trips-proxy.php:1350
msgid "The cache has been emptied."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1 and 2: the start and the end of the emphasis on "is"
#: includes/trips-proxy.php:1389
#, php-format
msgid "Every trip published in SilexGIS has a link of its own. The link %1$sis%2$s the key to it: whoever has it sees the page. That is why it is kept here, on the server, and not in the page the visitor reads."
msgstr ""

#: includes/trips-proxy.php:1396
msgid "A link saved here is public from that moment."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the address a link is read at through this site
#: includes/trips-proxy.php:1400
#, php-format
msgid "The token never leaves the server, but what the installation shows through it — the trip, the party, the positions — can be read through this site by anybody who knows or guesses the link's name (%s), whether the page that uses it is published, a draft or protected by a password."
msgstr ""

#: includes/trips-proxy.php:1401
msgctxt "a link's name, in an address"
msgid "name"
msgstr ""

#: includes/trips-proxy.php:1410
msgid "The installation's address"
msgstr ""

#: includes/trips-proxy.php:1413
msgid "https://example.org"
msgstr ""

#: includes/trips-proxy.php:1415
msgid "No path after it — only the scheme and the domain; whatever follows the domain is not kept. On saving, the installation is asked once for each link, and the message says what it answered."
msgstr ""

#: includes/trips-proxy.php:1420
msgid "Links"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: the form of a line, 2: the configuration's field, 3 to 5: the characters named
#: includes/trips-proxy.php:1428
#, php-format
msgid "One per line, in the form %1$s. The name appears in the page's configuration (%2$s) and may hold only letters without diacritics, digits, %3$s and %4$s, 40 characters at most; the token never leaves the server. Lines that begin with %5$s are notes and are kept as they were written. A line that cannot be understood stops the save and is named in the message: nothing is lost in silence."
msgstr ""

#: includes/trips-proxy.php:1429
msgid "name = token"
msgstr ""

#: includes/trips-proxy.php:1439
msgctxt "the name of another cave's links, as in other-1"
msgid "other"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: the ending of a name, 2 and 3: two names of one cave's links, 4 and 5: two of another cave's
#: includes/trips-proxy.php:1442
#, php-format
msgid "The links of one cave carry the same name followed by %1$s (%2$s, %3$s, …) and form a group. The archive and the tracks are asked for through the first link of the group that answers, beginning with the one that answered last: a revoked or expired link does not hide the archive while the group still has a valid one. The list of the followed trips is asked for through the link the page names, because the installation places the parties on the survey of the link that asks; only when that one stops answering does the list come through another link of the group, and the parties measured on another survey then appear without a position on the model; a link that refused the list is asked, for an hour, only after the others. Another cave's links get another name (%4$s, %5$s): a group never answers through another group's links. A name without %1$s is a group of its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/trips-proxy.php:1443
msgid "-number"
msgstr ""

#: includes/trips-proxy.php:1459 includes/trips-proxy.php:1466
msgid "Empty the cache"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the name of the button that empties the cache
#: includes/trips-proxy.php:1465
#, php-format
msgid "The installation's answers are kept for a short time (a link's trip and the list of the followed trips 20 s, the archive 5 min, a finished trip's track 1 min). A corrected report, a revoked link or a cave made protected shows on the page after that long at the latest. The reader's browser may keep an answer as well, but for 20 s at most and never beyond the time the copy here has left: the two do not add up beyond the times above. A refusal by the installation is remembered for 20 s. If two different reads in a row get no answer, the installation is not asked for 20 s; if one and the same read gets no answer twice in a row — a long track, say — only that read is not made for 20 s, and the rest goes on. %s deletes the copies on this server at once; a browser that has just read an answer may still show it for 20 s at most. Saving empties it as well."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: a header's name, 2: a file's name, 3, 5 and 6: settings of the installation, 4: a setting of its web server, 7: a network mask
#: includes/trips-proxy.php:1474
#, php-format
msgid "The installation counts requests per address, and every reader reaches it through this server, so as one single address. That is why this server sends the reader's address in %1$s; the installation takes it into account only if its operator declares this server a trusted proxy, in the installation's %2$s file: %3$s (one more than without this site: 3 under the TLS overlay, where the value is changed in the overlay's file and the address is also added to %4$s in the Caddyfile), %5$s the installation's Compose network (naming a network replaces the default list) and %6$s the address this server makes its requests from, with %7$s. Without these settings nothing changes. On shared hosting that address belongs to every site on the same server: declared trusted, any of them can present any address to the installation."
msgstr ""
